    takeawaysLabel: `Takeaways`,
    /* Seven. Not a summary of the record above but the things the record has
       taught us to hold to — the terms the next six years get run on. */
    takeaways: [
      { head: `Stewardship`, body: `A room is not run, it is kept. The work is caring for the people in it and showing up again the week after. It is the least visible thing this department does.` },
      { head: `Give everyone a role`, body: `Belonging comes with responsibility. The people who stayed are the ones who were handed a place — to talk, to give, to contribute. Hand someone a part and they move from the edge of the room to the middle of it.` },
      { head: `Go in not knowing`, body: `The program works when the subject arrives in the room rather than ahead of it. We don’t over-rehearse and we don’t over-plan. We trust each other, and we trust the room to find the thing worth saying.` },
      { head: `Keep it casual`, body: `Formality filters, and it filters out exactly the people a community like this is for. Nothing here should need preparing for, or dressing for, or qualifying for.` },
      { head: `Nothing performed, nothing owed`, body: `This is not a networking event and it is not a stage. The relationships that have lasted are the ones where nobody was selling and nobody was being watched. We laugh about the policy we put in to protect it: no networking allowed.` },
      { head: `Bridge the generations`, body: `We hold a space for people across generations, experience levels and interests, and give them somewhere to exist within. A legacy has to be handed to people who were not there at the start.` }
    ],

